  ],
  "notes": "A WMTS KVP endpoint rather than a REST tile path, so the whole request is in the query string and {z}/{y}/{x} appear as TILEMATRIX, TILEROW and TILECOL. This entry names the PM tile matrix set, which is IGN's own, and PM_0_19 is where the z19 ceiling is stated. Recipes pointing at wxs.ign.fr are still widely published and no longer work. Depth is real to z19 over metropolitan France and over the overseas departments - Guadeloupe, Martinique, Saint-Martin and Saint-Barthelemy among them - and the service also answers at world scale far outside France, which is a backdrop rather than a statement of coverage. WHERE IT HOLDS NOTHING IT SAYS SO THREE DIFFERENT WAYS across one region's build range: a flat navy sea fill at z10 to z12, the flat white JPEG declared above at z13 to z16, and honest 404s appearing from about z14. That white is the fingerprint - 1651 bytes, one md5, confirmed byte identical offshore of Guadeloupe and offshore of Corsica, 1400 km and two projection grids apart. The navy is deliberately NOT declared: over water it reads as water and it has not been confirmed on unrelated ground. Coverage is a coastal buffer about one z15 tile wide, so it closes over bays and inlets completely and leaves open coast marginal, and its edge follows a metric delivery grid rather than a tile boundary - which means tiles along that edge are part imagery and part white, and no fingerprint can reach those.",
